{"chapter": "spaces", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03FO", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4786739b94903ba19c58e757d903d6c99d490ad8a152ca7a43edb5e0df7aff66", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we briefly discuss what happens when we change big sites.\nThe upshot is that we can always enlarge the big site at will, hence we\nmay assume any set of schemes we want to consider is contained in the big\nfppf site over which we consider our algebraic space. Here is a precise\nstatement of the result.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d345bf993b10e3663ced7438648d60abd1f8c9fffa329a1afb8f8ccee292964d", "unit_id": "tag:03FO:prose-0001"}
